I collapsed the null check into a single short-circuit return so the common (field present) path avoids the extra branch and duplicated return, letting the compiler emit tighter code.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsTimestampValid() const
    {
        const Field* const field = GetField(253);
        return (FIT_NULL != field) ? field->IsValueValid() : FIT_FALSE;
    }
```